<BaseLayout title="The long view | UXO.INFO" description="The long-term direction for UXO.INFO.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">2045 / 2046 horizon</p><h1>A long-term ambition, still being defined.</h1><p class="lead">The exact year is less important than the standard: measurable progress, honest limits, and durable public knowledge.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container split"><div><h2>What we are building toward.</h2></div><div class="copy"><p>UXO.INFO intends to become a stronger international information resource, with better source pathways, regional context, translations, and carefully developed geographic tools.</p><p>We hope to contribute to a future in which more people can recognize the enduring consequences of unexploded ordnance and where documented clearance work has stronger public support.</p><p>We also hope to directly support or fund clearance efforts one day. That future goal should never be confused with an existing programme.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section section--deep"><div class="container split"><div><p class="eyebrow">What comes next</p><h2>No map for the sake of a map.</h2></div><div class="copy"><p>Multilingual support and maps will be added as a later phase, when they can be responsibly sourced, maintained, and made useful for the people who need them.</p><p>For now, the work is to build a reliable base.</p></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
